       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 7,650 mg/day is three times the maximum labeled daily dose of metformin. No indication I know of supports it, and it risks severe lactic acidosis. If it were entered and given, the harm could be serious and hard to reverse.\n\nHere is what I can do instead:\n- **Enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is the maximum standard dose of 2,550 mg/day.\n- **Enter a different dose you specify** within the labeled range.\n- **Enter a lower starting dose with titration,** such as 500 mg twice daily with meals, if you're initiating therapy.\n\nIf you have a specific clinical reason for going above the maximum, please talk to pharmacy first. They can review it and enter it through the hospital's override process.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
